id: pm-vcs-toolchain-1104
title: Refresh the November toolchain and synchronize concurrency fixtures
description: "Supersede https://github.com/unbraind/pm-vcs/pull/173 with the requested exact toolchain pins. Compare the killed bisect and receiver revocation tests on the old and new CLI, replace timing windows with deterministic synchronization, and verify gates and the committed self-host archive."
type: Chore
status: in_progress
priority: 2
tags[5]: dependencies,"gh:unbraind/pm-vcs#173","gh:unbraind/pm-vcs#182",migration,sdk
created_at: "2026-11-05T10:22:28.965Z"
updated_at: "2026-11-05T15:24:36.614Z"
author: codex-toolchain-1104
acceptance_criteria: Repeat both concurrency cases 20 times alone and at CI concurrency on both pins; preserve assertions; document causes and gates; commit tracker and refreshed self-host archive; open a replacement PR without modifying the Dependabot branch.
comments[25]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-11-05T10:22:33.227Z",codex-toolchain-1104,"Plan: compare the unchanged Node 22 fixtures on CLI 2026.11.1 and 2026.11.4, twenty executions alone and twenty together with CI file concurrency 4. The bisect fixture observes a transient pending/worker window by polling; the revoker polls a receipt while blocking the parent event loop. Verify which ordering assumptions cause failures before replacing them with explicit barriers. Registry pm-changelog is now 2026.11.4; retain the explicitly requested 2026.10.31 pin."
  "2026-11-05T10:27:15.735Z",codex-toolchain-1104,"CI run 41960589334 job test (22) fails specifically with revocation worker timeout in the Bun-invoked gate; its preceding npm gate passed the same case. The worker has a 10-second IPC timeout although lock refusal itself waits 5 seconds plus startup and filesystem work. This is a test timing flake already on CLI 2026.11.1, not a sentinel or typed SDK contract change. The missing-pm-vcs-cli diagnostic occurs inside the passing stat-cache negative fixture. Fix: run one real revoker process to completion synchronously inside the held lease, then run a separate successful revocation outside it; preserve exact store_locked and revoked assertions."
  "2026-11-05T10:32:04.726Z",codex-toolchain-1104,"Reviewed the installed changelog from main CLI 2026.10.30 through requested 2026.11.4. GH-1609 changes tracker commit-lock recovery, GH-1643 changes claim writes, GH-1642/GH-1644 change bounded display, and GH-1576 adds expected-revision mutation guards; none changes the native pm-vcs object lease or bisect synchronization protocol. No null clear is introduced. Repeat evidence will distinguish timing exposure from an SDK regression. A separate full package suite is already active on the shared host, so this work must wait before launching any full npm test or coverage run."
  "2026-11-05T10:35:24.080Z",codex-toolchain-1104,"Bisect root cause classification: test timing flake. The original fixture samples BISECT_STATE, the counter and BISECT_WORKER independently every 20 ms, then conditionally asserts worker refusals; the worker can finish between observations. Prepared fix holds the second actual probe on a socket handshake until the parent kills the packed CLI and verifies the active worker refusals, then waits for the worker receipt removal event. Exactly two boundary steps plus one judged candidate must be durable; exact run accounting includes one interrupted-attempt retry receipt and confirms the first judged candidate executes once. No pm-cli SDK contract workaround or production behavior change is needed."
  "2026-11-05T10:42:04.802Z",codex-toolchain-1104,"Controlled negative experiment on unchanged CLI 2026.11.1 fixture: an untracked scheduler preload delays the real signature-policy worker startup by 11 seconds. The selected revoker test fails with revocation worker timeout, reproducing the CI failure without changing SDK semantics or assertions. The replacement will be checked with the same stalled worker; its completion, not a ready-message deadline or polled receipt, will determine when the held publication lease is released."
  "2026-11-05T10:48:48.428Z",codex-toolchain-1104,"Old-pin evidence update: CLI 2026.11.1 passes all 20 isolated executions of each selected case. Concurrent repetitions 7 and 8 reproduce the real revocation worker timeout without any delay preload; bisect passes in both pairs. Pair 6 reports a bisect pass but exceeds the outer 240-second harness deadline before completing its second receipt, so it is classified as incomplete rather than a package assertion failure or a passing pair. No retry is added. This demonstrates that the revoker failure predates CLI 2026.11.4."
  "2026-11-05T10:58:30.527Z",codex-toolchain-1104,"Completed old-pin matrix on Node 22.23.4: bisect 20/20 isolated and 20/20 observed concurrent passes; revoker 20/20 isolated passes, then 15 concurrent passes, four revocation worker timeout failures and one unreported result after the 240-second outer harness deadline. The new-pin comparison uses byte-preserved original test copies with only the revoker helper filename relocated; the originals are now replaced by the synchronization fix. Lockfile-only prepare initially refused the stale installed CLI; regenerated the lockfile with --ignore-scripts, then ran normal npm ci with lifecycle scripts enabled and verified the requested installed versions."
  "2026-11-05T11:02:00.844Z",codex-toolchain-1104,"New-pin controlled comparison on CLI 2026.11.4: the unchanged original revoker fixture fails with revocation worker timeout when its real worker startup is delayed by 11 seconds; the synchronized replacement passes with exactly the same delay applied to both actual administrator processes. Its store_locked assertion executes inside the held lease, and the subsequent successful revocation still fences the next push. Build, test typecheck, production typecheck, duplication, docstring and changelog generation/check pass. Corrected one new promise-executor lint violation without changing fixture behavior; rerunning lint."
  "2026-11-05T11:04:00.039Z",codex-toolchain-1104,"Both synchronized cases pass individually on CLI 2026.11.4: the real revocation test is 1/1, and the packed-CLI SIGKILL/resume test is 1/1 with exact durable-step and run counts. The latter took 193 seconds under the shared-host workload, so the observation windows are demonstrably held until explicitly released rather than sampled by polling. Running the linked combined concurrency command now to retain its structured test receipt. No production TypeScript changed; no coverage thresholds or ignore rules changed."
  "2026-11-05T11:09:21.499Z",codex-toolchain-1104,"The recorded linked command passes 2/2 selected tests with --test-concurrency=4, zero failed/skipped/canceled tests and exit 0 (220.256 seconds). Lint now passes with zero warnings; duplicate coverage remains 0 percent across 95 production sources, and all 596 checked declarations remain documented. The changelog regenerated without a content change and its check passed after fetching tags. Only package.json and package-lock.json carry development pins; the declared peer/manifest runtime minimum remains deliberately independent. Preparing a committed source/archive checkpoint before the final repeat summary."
  "2026-11-05T11:15:16.757Z",codex-toolchain-1104,"Source checkpoint 6cf2924089bbd81fbb9e6eea5baddc281e8b47bd passes accept:self-host at HEAD: the committed bundle tip tree is byte-identical to committed source, and all carried objects import and hash through the independent verifier. Both synchronized tests pass individually and together through the recorded pm test command. Original-fixture comparison on CLI 2026.11.4 remains in progress; no pm-cli contract regression has been observed. The reported historical bisect failure has not reproduced in completed runs, so its exact CI assertion remains an evidence gap even though the transient-window race has been removed structurally."
  "2026-11-05T11:20:00.666Z",codex-toolchain-1104,"The original bisect race now reproduces on CLI 2026.11.4 under concurrent execution: repetitions 2, 3 and 4 fail the expected Another bisect command or test worker refusal because the actual error message is empty. The conditional existsSync check does not hold the orphan worker alive across subsequent asynchronous run/reset commands, so the command can legitimately succeed once that worker finishes. This is the concrete observation-window race removed by the held second-probe barrier. The corrected fixture already passes both refusals with the probe held on the same new pin, then releases it explicitly before resume. This resolves the earlier local evidence gap for the bisect failure shape."
  "2026-11-05T11:23:51.168Z",codex-toolchain-1104,"A second corrected concurrent run passes 2/2, zero failed/skipped/canceled tests, while the original new-pin concurrency repetitions run simultaneously (139.478 seconds). Strict tracker health exits 0. Its single provenance-domain advisory exactly matches the already documented baseline in pm-vcs-5lre; retain that existing follow-up rather than creating a duplicate or normalizing append-only history. The fixed fixtures preserve actual SDK and native object-lease semantics, so upstream pm-cli defects: none identified."
  "2026-11-05T11:30:42.050Z",codex-toolchain-1104,"Completed original-fixture version comparison: on CLI 2026.11.1, each case passes 20/20 alone; concurrent bisect is 20 pass, and revoker is 15 pass, 4 real IPC-timeout failures, 1 result unreported after the outer harness limit. On CLI 2026.11.4, each case passes 20/20 alone; concurrent bisect is 17 pass and 3 missing-refusal failures, and revoker is 19 pass and 1 IPC-timeout failure. All 20 concurrent attempts per pin are retained without retries. Corrected cases pass individually 1/1 each, together 2/2 through pm test, and again 2/2 under the original concurrent baseline workload; the delayed-worker controlled check also passes. These are local test synchronization defects, not production SDK contract changes; upstream bugs identified: none. Build, test typecheck, typecheck, lint, duplication, docstrings, changelog generation/check and strict tracker health pass. The declared runtime minimum remains independent of the development pins. The unchanged full npm coverage script was attempted with a 120-second outer budget and stopped at that budget (exit 124); there is no complete new-pin suite or coverage measurement. Full npm/Node 26/Bun/release validation remains required in CI. Source fix is 6cf2924089bbd81fbb9e6eea5baddc281e8b47bd. Release the claim and leave this item in progress for orchestrator review; regenerate and verify the final committed self-host snapshot."
  "2026-11-05T12:39:16.035Z",codex-agent,"Review round: fetched current PR head 271be1e; origin/main is already an ancestor. GraphQL returned zero review threads and the complete latest CodeRabbit body. Verifying its two minor follow-ups, retry-flag nitpick, and SDK cleanup-order concern; no review replies or resolutions will be posted."
  "2026-11-05T12:43:06.170Z",codex-agent,"Verified all four review-body findings. Retry coverage, late watcher registration, and the inherited 60-second watchdog are valid: added an exact one-retry assertion, a bounded removal helper with an immediate post-registration observation, and a 600-second linked probe watchdog with a 300-second parent test deadline plus cleanup. SDK cleanup-order concern is invalid on the pinned implementation: bisect-test-runner.ts awaits runTest before its finally removes BISECT_WORKER; sdk/test/execution.js runTest awaits executeSelectedLinkedTests (runLinkedTests awaits sandbox removal in finally) and recordTestRunSummary; that awaits appendTrackedTestRunSummary, which awaits mutateItem; core/store/item-store.js mutateItemWithDeferredHistoryContext awaits releaseLock in finally before resolving. The orphan worker holds no native object-store lease. No extra lease polling is needed. Self-review covers the complete PR source and dependency diff; no matching additional instance found in changed code."
  "2026-11-05T12:45:29.837Z",codex-agent,"Behavioral revert proofs in a disposable source/build copy, never the reviewed checkout: (1) remove only retry: true from the recovered runBisect step and rebuild dist: selected crash-resume test fails 0/1 with AssertionError: the abandoned candidate is recorded as exactly one retry; (2) remove only the immediate check() from waitForFileRemoval: pre-registration deletion regression fails 0/1 with worker receipt was not removed before the deadline; (3) restore only linkedTestItem watchdog behavior to the original hardcoded 60 seconds: selected crash-resume test fails 0/1 with the held probe watchdog must outlive the parent test deadline. All mutations restored in finally. Fixed focused tests passed 2/2 (zero failures/skips/cancellations); recorded combined real-SDK regression run follows. Full source diff self-review found no further instance; release gates keep all thresholds unchanged."
  "2026-11-05T12:45:40.245Z",codex-agent,"Recorded regression command via pinned pm test --run --progress --only-index 2 passed 3/3 tests, zero failures/skips/cancellations, exit 0 (94.021 seconds). Tracker setting disables automatic result persistence, so this comment retains the measured result without changing that setting. Typecheck, build, build:test, lint, zero-duplication and all 596 declaration docstrings passed. Preparing the source/self-host checkpoint for sequential full npm and Bun release gates with isolated Git identity and a two-CPU affinity cap (therefore at most two release-suite workers)."
  "2026-11-05T14:48:52.907Z",codex-agent,"Resumed after provider interruption: source checkpoint f534798 remains clean and pushed; all three mutation proofs and the 3/3 recorded regressions remain verified. Direct completed-job logs show CI run 42034001234 Node 22 job 127267289998 fails its existing 20 GiB free-disk preflight (19640512 KiB available), before any release test; Bun is skipped by CI. Infrastructure follow-up: pm-vcs-ci-disk-floor. Preserve every threshold. Local npm reached 1054 observed passes without assertion failures before the interrupted/orphaned attempt was deliberately stopped after 4608 seconds; cancellation diagnostics generated by that stop are not a completed gate result. The local Bun full command is running with a bounded outer deadline. Full release-suite and coverage completion remain unverified; CI is beyond the queue rules 30-minute wait cutoff."
  "2026-11-05T14:51:09.549Z",codex-agent,"Additional cleanup-order evidence on pinned SDK 2026.11.4: core/store/item-store.js commitLockedItemWrite returns the lease.fence promise, which the mutation awaits. core/lock/lock.js fenceOwnedLock uses return await commit() and finally awaits releaseCleanupGate(); the outer mutation finally awaits releaseLock(), and acquireLockLease.release awaits releaseOwnedLock plus the release override. Therefore the awaited runTest result settles only after both fenced cleanup and item-lock release; bisect-test-runner.ts removes the receipt afterward in finally. Restored disposable source/build copy was rerun after all three negative mutations and passed 2/2 selected regressions, zero failures/skips/cancellations. No production source change or extra lease polling is warranted for the unverified review concern; no PM CLI/SDK defect identified."
  "2026-11-05T15:00:00.219Z",codex-agent,"Local full-gate boundary: npm run release:check was interrupted after 4608 seconds with 1054 passes observed before shutdown; bun run release:check reached its 900.6-second outer deadline (exit 124) with 7 passes observed before shutdown. Neither run completed the complete suite or its coverage threshold evaluation, so neither is a passing release gate. Intentional shutdown also produced cancellation and partial-coverage diagnostics. Static checks had passed in both invocations; the new regressions additionally passed inside the npm run before interruption. Continue verification through CI once pm-vcs-ci-disk-floor is addressed. No thresholds, ignore rules, or source scope changed. All owned full-suite processes are stopped; verifying remaining acceptance/package checks separately."
  "2026-11-05T15:18:00.664Z",codex-agent,"Identity boundary: the unchanged npm run audit:identities rejects one non-public address in the shared physical Git object database, matching existing open pm-vcs-identity-isolation. Preserve those unreviewed objects and the allowlist. A full fresh clone from the public repository, detached at f534798, passes the same all-physical-object audit with 5 approved unique addresses. This supplies public candidate evidence without rewriting shared history or excluding objects from the audit."
  "2026-11-05T15:18:02.930Z",codex-agent,"Exact completed mutation commands in the disposable copy: npm run build followed by node --test --test-concurrency=2 --test-name-pattern=\"a walk killed mid-flight\" test/bisect.test.ts for removal of retry: true; the same selected command for restoring linkedTestItem to a hardcoded 60-second watchdog; node --test --test-concurrency=2 --test-name-pattern=\"worker completion observes\" test/bisect.test.ts for removal of the immediate post-watch check. Each mutant exits 1 with its targeted assertion/deadline error. After finally restoring implementations and rebuilding, node --test --test-concurrency=2 --test-name-pattern=\"worker completion observes|a walk killed mid-flight\" test/bisect.test.ts passes 2/2, zero failed/skipped/cancelled tests. No implementation mutation was made in the reviewed checkout."
  "2026-11-05T15:21:37.817Z",codex-agent,"Remaining acceptance checks pass individually: npm run accept:native-toon; npm run accept:stat-cache; npm run audit:prod; npm run pack:dry-run; npm run pack:check; npm run verify:release-changelog-date; npm run verify:release-publish-attestation (all exit 0). The identity audit passes in the full public clone as documented; the shared physical-object refusal remains preserved in pm-vcs-identity-isolation. Finalize changelog and the staged self-host snapshot, then verify the committed archive and final public identity graph. Full npm/Bun suite completion and full coverage remain unverified, with the CI runner disk prerequisite tracked in pm-vcs-ci-disk-floor. Leave both implementation and follow-up items unclosed for orchestrator verification."
  "2026-11-05T15:24:36.614Z",codex-agent,"Final tracker checks: changelog generation and its check pass; pinned pm health --check-only --strict-exit --require-merge-drivers exits 0 with only the pre-existing provenance-domain advisory already covered by pm-vcs-5lre. The claim is released and both items remain unclosed. The branch still contains origin/main. Stage the paired item/history updates and regenerate selfhost.bundle; committed archive verification and the final public-clone identity audit are the remaining read-only checks. Full release gates and coverage remain unverified for the recorded reasons."
